/-!
# Algebraic models of multiplier ideals

Blueprint `claude-gagamult2:sections-algebraic`, `claude-gagamult2:mult-alg`.

Let `X` be smooth projective over `ℂ`, `(L, H)` a metrized algebraic line bundle on `X`
(`a` a rank-one atlas of `L`), and `(L, H)^an` its analytification
(`SGPT.NAPotential.GAGAMult.schemeHermitianLineBundle`).

* `SchemeSectionsAlgebraic j`: **GAGA for the sections of `L^j`** (the statement, not proved
  here; lane SERRE-GAGA): every holomorphic section `s` of `((L, H)^an)^{⊗ j}` is the
  analytification of an algebraic section `σ ∈ H⁰(X, L^{⊗ j})`, i.e. in every algebraic frame
  `α` of the atlas, the coefficient of `s` in `α^{⊗ j}` is the analytic function of the
  algebraic coefficient of `σ` in `α^{⊗ j}`.
* `sectionZeroIdealSheaf_le_algebraization`: the algebraic ideal sheaf generated by such a
  `σ` (Bing–Wang's `sectionZeroIdealSheaf`, the image of `σ : L^{-j} → 𝒪_X`) is contained in
  the algebraic model `alg 𝓘(cφ)` as soon as `∫_X |σ^an|² e^{-cφ} < ∞`.
* **`multiplierIdeal_le_analytificationIdeal_algebraization`**: if `H` has positive curvature
  (`H.curvature a` is a Kähler form) and GAGA holds for the sections of `L^j`, `j ≫ 0`, then for
  every quasi-psh `φ` on `X(ℂ)` and `c > 0`, `𝓘(cφ) ⊆ alg(𝓘(cφ))^an`.  Proof: Siu's uniform
  global generation for a fixed weight (`siuGlobalGeneration_fixedWeight`) generates `𝓘(cφ)_x`
  by the coefficients of the finite-`L²` global sections of `L^j`; by GAGA they are algebraic,
  and their algebraic coefficients lie in `alg 𝓘(cφ)`.
* `multiplierIdealAlgebraic_of_positive`: hence `MultiplierIdealAlgebraic`, and
  `analytificationIdeal_algebraization_multiplierIdeal`: `alg(𝓘(cφ))^an = 𝓘(cφ)`.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false
set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false

noncomputable section

